From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] WindowManager: no animation at all when the animation scales
 are 0

PW3 ships with the window, transition and animator scales at 0 (e-paper).
Scaled to 0 ms, an animation still applies its final transformation for one
frame: Animation.getTransformation() returns true once more after it has
ended. Opening an app from the launcher (task_open_exit) thus composed one
frame with the launcher scaled to 90%, at 60% opacity, moved down 10%, over
the animation's black background. The PW3 composer does not scale layers, so
that frame went to SwiftShader, which spent 10-23 s of CPU on it while
SurfaceFlinger could serve nothing else: WeRead's cold start took 24.5-25.8 s
and its window had not appeared 20 s after the launch (PW3 Android, Test V48).

With a scale of 0 an app transition and a window animation now take the path
of a frozen display: the windows change visibility without any animation.
Battery saver's mAnimationsDisabled reaches the same scales and the same path.

